# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) for local development, and set the same
# variable in your host's environment — on Vercel: Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables. Vite substitutes it at BUILD time, so changing it on
# the host needs a redeploy before it takes effect.
#
# Without it the contact form in the Colophon's About tab is not rendered at
# all. See "Contact form" in README.md.
#
# EITHER NAME WORKS. `VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT` is the Vite convention;
# `CONTACT_ENDPOINT` is accepted too, for hosts whose dashboard will not take
# the first one. `envPrefix` in vite.config.ts is what lets the shorter name
# through — without that entry Vite would not expose it and the form would
# quietly go on not rendering.
#
# This is a form id, not an address. It is public by design and gives nothing
# away; the address it forwards to lives with the form service and never
# reaches the browser. There is no `mailto:` option, on purpose.
VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx
# CONTACT_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx
